Goal: Add a deterministic, local-first code snippet generator that scaffolds the AI-assisted decomposition flow (CLI handler, decomposer service, and task-store persistence) consistent with existing TaskForge architecture.
Decisions: Bun + TypeScript CLI with a lightweight parser (commander) and thin CLI layer delegating to src/commands/* and src/services/*; Persist tasks as a versioned JSON store (TaskStoreFile { version: 1; tasks: TaskRecord[] }) with atomic saves via temp-file + rename; Keep runtime validation local and lightweight (manual guards or a small schema lib) to ensure persisted JSON matches v1 shape; Make the snippet generator deterministic and local-first (keyword -> template) with a clear interface to swap in a live AI provider later; Separate concerns: decomposer, snippet-generator, summarizer, and task-mutations live in services so CLI remains minimal
